cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TScert, please cite it as below."
title: "TScert: a sound core for TypeScript"
abstract: >-
  TScert is a research verifier for type claims about TypeScript programs. A
  producer proposes the types of a function's expressions; an independent
  checker, whose soundness is proved in Lean, accepts the function only when a
  certificate checks against the function's translation into a formal model.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Calcagno
    given-names: Cristiano
repository-code: "https://github.com/cristianoc/TScert"
url: "https://github.com/cristianoc/TScert"
version: "0.9"
date-released: "2026-11-03"
keywords:
  - TypeScript
  - type safety
  - formal verification
  - Lean 4
  - proof-carrying code
